      "problem": "What is the supremum of the set $C=\\{-4,\\,3,\\,-2,\\,1\\}?$\n\n$sup(C)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The supremum of a set $C$ is the smallest upper bound of $C.$\n\nIf $C$ is a finite set, the supremum of $C$ equals its maximum. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sup(C) & =max\\{-4,\\,3,\\,-2,\\,1\\}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
